sections: INPUT, OUTPUT, COMMENTS, STAMPS!!
{

	!! ----
	!! FOOP-55 §9.2 — concatenation ergonomics, simple to complex.
	!! Each statement names the §9.2 row it exercises. The rule: when a
	!! concatenation is WRITTEN, each constituent is classified and that
	!! classification decides the marking the compiler supplies, so the
	!! common case needs no marks written by hand.
	!! §9.2 row: BRANE constituent -> SFF-marked by the compiler.
	!! Two brane literals flatten to the union of their statements.
	!! ----
	brane_pair = {1, 2} {3, 4};

	!! ----
	!! §9.2 row: MARKER already written -> compiled AS WRITTEN, no second
	!! mark added. All three spellings below must agree: the Foolisher's
	!! mark stands, and the compiler neither doubles nor downgrades it.
	!! ----
	mark_none = {5, 7} {q = 1;};
	mark_sf = {5, 7} <{q = 1;}>;
	mark_sff = {5, 7} <<{q = 1;}>>;

	!! ----
	!! The same three with a CONTEXT-DEPENDENT body. <<#-1>> resolves to the
	!! statement one before it, so q picks up 7 in every spelling. This is
	!! the case that would expose a silent SF/SFF downgrade if one existed.
	!! ----
	ctx_none = {5, 7} {q = <<#-1>>;};
	ctx_sf = {5, 7} <{q = <<#-1>>;}>;
	ctx_sff = {5, 7} <<{q = <<#-1>>;}>>;

	!! ----
	!! §9.2 row: SEARCH constituent -> SF-marked by the compiler.
	!! "Search, any of them" is deliberately flat: every search form takes
	!! the same treatment. Three forms follow, all resolving to the same
	!! two-statement brane.
	!! ----
	src = {8, 9};

	!! ----
	!! uncontexted UNANCHORED search by name
	!! ----
	search_unanchored = {0} src;

	!! ----
	!! uncontexted ANCHORED search — anchor resolves through to a brane
	!! ----
	holder = {inner = {10, 11};};
	search_anchored = {0} holder.inner;

	!! ----
	!! Positional search as a constituent needs an explicit mark. Written
	!! bare, `{0} #-2` is NOT a concatenation at all: `#` binds POSTFIX and
	!! takes the preceding `{0}` as its ANCHOR, so it reads as an anchored
	!! seek into a one-statement brane and settles NK (nothing at -2). The
	!! mark makes the seek its own constituent, and it stays UNANCHORED.
	!! @agent NOTE: `search_index = {0} <<#-2>>;` is deliberately ABSENT.
	!! It settles WOCONSTANIC — the marked search stays ECONSTANIC and the
	!! concatenation never completes — which is defect D9 (FOOP-55 §D9,
	!! plan 3G.5), NOT a §9.2 marking question. It is the same signature as
	!! `{a={1,2}, b=<<#-2>>, c= a b}`. Add it here once D9 is fixed; this
	!! file is the §9.2 baseline and must not carry a known-red line.
	!! The postfix reading, kept as the control: `#` binds POSTFIX and takes
	!! the preceding brane as its ANCHOR, so this is an anchored seek into
	!! the brane (finding 9), not a concatenation at all. That is why a bare
	!! `{0} #-2` cannot serve as a "search constituent" example.
	!! ----
	seek_is_postfix = {0, 9, 8}#-2;

	!! ----
	!! §9.2 row: CONCATENATION constituent -> SFF-marked, "treated exactly
	!! as a brane". A nested written concatenation must FLATTEN, not NK.
	!! Before this rule was implemented the second inner concatenation was
	!! dropped and the whole outer expression went NK.
	!! ----
	nested_concat = (({1}{2}) ({3}{4}));

	!! ----
	!! Deeper nesting, three constituents per side.
	!! ----
	nested_deep = (({1}{2}{3}) ({4}{5}{6}));

	!! ----
	!! §9.2 row: OPERATOR constituent -> NK, with a reason naming the kind
	!! ("cannot concatenate number"). The operator really is a constituent
	!! here because the parentheses make it one.
	!! ----
	operator_nk = {1} (2 + 3);

	!! ----
	!! §9.4(e) control: a single-element {1} is a BRANE LITERAL, not a
	!! one-constituent concatenation. §9.2 governs written concatenations of
	!! two or more constituents, so none of the marking rules apply here.
	!! ----
	single_is_brane = {1};

	!! ----
	!! @agent NOTE on `worked` below: its `b` settles WOCONSTANIC, and that
	!! is NOT a §9.2 marking failure. `{c = {e f g}}$` yields a BRANE, and
	!! `brane + 1` has no meaning, so the Op+ never settles. Isolated:
	!! `{c = {e f g}}$` alone flattens correctly to {{21;22;23}}, and
	!! `{c = 5}$ + 1` gives 6 — only brane-plus-number hangs. Arguably it
	!! should settle NK ("cannot add a brane") rather than stay WOCONSTANIC;
	!! that is an operator question, filed outside §9.2. The line is kept
	!! verbatim from §9.3 because the point under test is the MARKING of its
	!! constituents, which is correct: {e f g} flattens and x/y resolve.
	!! §9.3 worked example — the complex interaction. The outer
	!! concatenation has two brane constituents, so both are SFF-marked.
	!! Inside the first, {e f g} is itself a written concatenation of three
	!! searches, so each of e, f and g is SF-marked; x and y are already
	!! marked by the Foolisher and are compiled as written.
	!! ----
	e = {21};
	f = {22};
	g = {23};
	aa = 24;
	bb = 25;
	worked = {b = {c = {e f g}}$ + 1; x = <aa>, y = <<bb>>} {'my_truth = 'True, 'my_falsehood = 'False};
}
!!
